  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Missing Migrants Project: Data, Research and Capacity Building on Migrant Deaths and Disappearances Worldwide</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project continues and builds on the work funded by Switzerland&#x2019;s FDFA over the past two years on the Missing Migrants Project (MMP), which is carried out by the International Organization for Migration&#x2019;s Global Migration Data Analysis Centre (GMDAC). The outputs of this next project phase will be threefold. Output 1 will ensure the continuation of the global data collection and monitoring of incidents of migrant deaths and disappearances worldwide through the global MMP team at GMDAC and the network of six data focal points in IOM regional offices. The second output will be to provide timely analysis of Missing Migrants Project data, through a series of 6 briefings that will look at regional data and global themes related to the topic of missing migrants. The third output will be to continue the work funded by Switzerland&#x2019;s FDFA regarding the needs and challenges faced by families of missing migrants in Ethiopia, Spain, the United Kingdom and Zimbabwe, by producing internal guidelines for IOM and conducting awareness trainings on how families of missing migrants can be better supported.</narrative>
  </description>
